          "title": "You'll want to know: le pare-brise",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le pare-brise — \"the windscreen\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Un caillou a cassé le pare-brise. A stone broke the windscreen."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The plural does not change: des pare-brise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pare-brise is built from parer 'to ward off' and brise 'breeze' (EtymDB): the glass that keeps the wind out. Parer goes back to Latin parāre 'to prepare' (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
